      "reason": "Build an inference-aligned stress-test suite that distinguishes reliance on recent intent from broad historical affinity. Use paired training-prefix targets, fixed candidates, recent-deletion versus count-matched deletion, and latest-item-preserving shuffles. Seek identity controls, injected-fault tests for MASK/readout errors, and user-clustered uncertainty; interpret perturbations as sensitivity rather than causal intent.",
      "query": "BERT4Rec sequential recommendation diagnostic benchmarks history perturbation recency order sensitivity metamorphic testing masked next item prediction 2024 2025 2026"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Connect qualitative rejection reasons to measurable ranking failures. Investigate evidence-linked annotation of the twenty training users’ recommendations for explicit willingness to choose, duplication, compatibility, quantity, and mood mismatch. Use only supplied feedback, histories, titles, descriptions, and timestamps; retain unknown judgments, measure annotation agreement and coverage, and avoid inferring latent traits or treating missing interactions as rejection.",
      "query": "recommendation evaluation explicit user feedback rejection reasons annotation rubric uncertainty abstention redundancy compatibility intent relevance 2024 2025 2026"
    },
    {
      "reason": "Develop an auditable explanation of how supervision reaches one BERT4Rec network. Resolve the observed fixed-branch versus Bernoulli documentation conflict using checkpoint-linked sampler provenance and exact loss accounting, then investigate sparse branch-gradient covariance and conflict probes by embedding and encoder component. Seek controls that separate context distribution, target normalization, and allocation effects without training auxiliary predictors or changing the host evaluator.",
      "query": "multi objective learning gradient covariance diagnostics task sampling allocation separate loss normalization gradient conflict provenance reproducibility 2024 2025 2026"
    }
  ]
